      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is understandable that when the larger system feels rigged, local solutions like therapy can feel like minor adjustments to a crisis. However, many counselors focus not just on fixing symptoms but on helping you rebuild agency and find meaning even within overwhelming constraints. You might not have control over the \"system,\" but you can still choose your perspective, set boundaries, and protect your well-being. This realization alone can be the first step toward breaking the cycle of feeling like a bystander to your own life.",
      "source": "target",
